{"strongs": "H0165", "word": "אֱהִי", "translit": "e.hi", "root": "אהד", "morph": "H:Adv", "pos": "adverb", "gloss": "where", "definition": "אֱהִי Hos 13:10 ; Hos 13:14 (twice in verse) adverb where ? = אֵי , אַיֵּה . So ᵐ5 ᵑ6 ᵑ9 ᵑ7 AW in Hos 13:10 , & ᵐ5 ᵑ6 (compare 1Cor 15:55 ) AW in Hos 13:14 . Taken by many of the older interpreters, and even by Ges in Hos 13:14 , as 1 singular imperfect with apocope of היה I would be: but this is less suited to the context, and the jussive form is an objection, being unusual with the 1 person", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB152')\">BDB152</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H165')\">H165</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB151')\">BDB151</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB153')\">BDB153</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אֱהִי</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Hos 13:10\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(28,13,10)\">Hos 13:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Hos 13:14\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(28,13,14)\">Hos 13:14</ref> (twice in verse) <b>adverb</b> <highlightword>where</highlightword> ? = <bdbheb>אֵי</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>אַיֵּה</bdbheb>. So <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Vg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ9</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('AW')\">AW</lookup> in <ref ref=\"Hos 13:10\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(28,13,10)\">Hos 13:10</ref>, &amp; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> (compare <ref ref=\"1Cor 15:55\" b=\"46\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"55\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"55\" onclick=\"bcv(46,15,55)\">1Cor 15:55</ref>) <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('AW')\">AW</lookup> in <ref ref=\"Hos 13:14\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(28,13,14)\">Hos 13:14</ref>. Taken by many of the older interpreters, and even by <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ges')\">Ges</lookup> in <ref ref=\"Hos 13:14\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(28,13,14)\">Hos 13:14</ref>, as 1 singular imperfect with apocope of <bdbheb>היה</bdbheb> <highlight>I would be:</highlight> but this is less suited to the context, and the jussive form is an objection, being unusual with the 1 person </p><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Hos 13:10", "book": "HOS", "chapter": 13, "verse": 10}, {"raw": "Hos 13:14", "book": "HOS", "chapter": 13, "verse": 14}, {"raw": "1Cor 15:55", "book": "1CO", "chapter": 15, "verse": 55}], "flagged": {"hebrew": ["אֱהִי", "אֵי", "אַיֵּה", "ᵐ5", "ᵑ6", "ᵑ9", "ᵑ7", "היה"], "aramaic": [], "greek": [], "translit": [], "abbreviations": ["AW", "Ges", "Sept", "Syr", "Tg", "Vg"]}, "covers": [], "bdbid": "BDB152", "source": "BDB", "testament": "OT"}